  "notes": [
    "Manuscript page 5; pencil foliation 367. Two proof methods are sketched: the classifying-space/Tor spectral sequence, with Eilenberg–Moore and “Steenrod - Rothenberger”; then “2) Methode de Serre”, “Comm Helv”, “1954”. The lower margin refers to a Springer symposium in honour of Steenrod and an “Article de May.” These references are transcribed, not researched.",
    "The normalization prefix N is visible before ZK; omitting it changes the object from the normalized complex to the simplicial free-abelian object. The lower bar construction has three face arrows. Counting the faces of a two-simplex confirms that three is coherent, but the scan decides their number. Both identifications (E_2 and the normalized complex to M) use ≃. The source’s mixed closing bracket at the upper right and omitted/shifted parentheses are retained. The first K in the final spectral sequence has F without p; no subscript is supplied from the expected coefficients.",
    "The crossed ⊗ZK expression and the separate crossed tensor before the lower H_* are distinct deletions. The circled ZK expression is live and doubly underlined. In the crowded lower bar term, the ambiguous n/x form is read as n using the same local K(F_p,n) notation, with medium confidence. No full spectral-sequence or homology calculation is claimed."
  ],
